WEBVTT

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:47.690
Warning!

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.790
An Aanval... No!

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.600
Hu... man?

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.180
The destroyer of countless Cerebrants.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.380
The demon soldier of the Gards-orm.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:07.610
Abyss.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:15.010
What the hell is this?

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.400
What are you doing, Kyo?!

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:37.570
Lu-shen!

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.550
Trying to run?!

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:52.730
Be careful!

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.530
This guy's stronger than
any enemy you've faced yet.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.670
Kyo?

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.530
Is it true?

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.930
That this is reality...
And the Gards-orm are...

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.100
human?

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.670
They're not human.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.810
They're artificial.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.650
We're the only humans here!

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.680
Artificial?

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.510
That guy?

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.620
Yes.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.560
The Garuda's having a tough time.
Kyo, move towards them.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.210
Why, you!

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.370
Quit smashin' my house!

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:51.520
I'm from Chiba-ken, pal, so don't mess with me!

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.680
This guy's super strong!

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.260
Main generator, damaged!

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.960
Weapon chamber coil, off-line!

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:07.430
I can't form our holonic armor, either!

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.640
- Damn you, Abyss...
- Leg-section signal transduction level now 15%!

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.100
Looks like it. May-yen!

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.210
Roger!

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.370
Activating Banishment Mode!

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:22.180
<i>Activating Banishment Mode.</i>
<i>Transmission commencing.</i>

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.050
Shizuno, be careful! There's more than one of...

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:36.730
It self-destructed?

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:39.370
We're only lightly damaged. No problem.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.240
Kyo, we should retreat as well.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.900
Run from them? Why?!

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.340
Because the enemy objective from the start was...

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.000
These guys bust up my place and
you expect me to leave them alone?!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.350
Kyo!

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.280
Where is he?!

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.020
Thermal reaction, behind the building!

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.950
What are you, a cockroach?!

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.360
Sorry, my mistake.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:10.660
Sin was hiding in Abyss's shadow!
There's two of them!

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.740
Hah! Trying to flank me, huh?

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:20.260
So, on the other side must be!

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.250
Wha?

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.750
No! Above us!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.840
No way!

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.560
Kyo! On our left!

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.970
You... son... of a... BITCH!!!

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.050
Shit! We hit each other!

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.560
No. We've lost, Kyo.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.350
Don't look!

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.790
They've already stolen it.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:15.420
Now the Zega's program data
is in the Gards-orm's hands.

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.430
S... Sempai...

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.140
Go to hell, Sin!

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.390
So, that's how it is?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.520
Does this look like a game to you?
Like an artificial world?

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:30.500
Like, am I really alive or not? Stuff like that.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:34.400
Personally, it doesn't matter to me which is which.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.550
Maybe both worlds are an illusion.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.320
However, if one world is reality,

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.480
then it follows that the other must be fiction.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.160
My place...

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:17.180
What the hell?

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.060
<i>It has to be.</i>

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.070
<i>This is reality.</i>

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:40.040
If those ruins are reality, then
what the hell am I looking at now?

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.600
A construct.

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.570
Wh-What are you doing here, Fosetta?

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.290
Oh, come on! You called us here, didn't you, Kyo?

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.950
To answer your questions.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.460
Oh. Is that what I did?

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.890
Okay, then answer me.
This is reality, right? It is, isn't it?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.020
It could be defined as reality,

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:08.360
but as an objective world which is changeable
by thought or action, then no, it is not.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.630
What? It's not?

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:15.810
But, my hand! In the other world, something
happened to it that should be impossible!

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:17.710
What was that?!

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:20.050
Because everything is a fabrication.

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.780
Not just the city, but the people, too.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:28.820
May I keep asking you questions?

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:33.120
Sure, but we're blocked from discussing any
more of the subject we've been talking about.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:38.130
If you have any questions about the weather
or diet tips, we're available 24 hours a day.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.900
What do you mean?!

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:42.890
Miss Shizuno is responsible for your case.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.600
We'd need to get her decision first.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:47.480
Sempai...

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:49.100
That's right! How is she?!

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.150
Miss Shizuno needs a bit more time to recover.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.210
The dry damage she suffered was substantial.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.820
We were late arriving here.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.480
If only we could have gotten there sooner.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.260
Look at her, after days of regeneration.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:07.830
Pitiful, huh?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.460
Well, it's a sight I've gotten used to.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.860
Chris...

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:19.330
Oh, sorry! I never know when
to keep my mouth shut, huh?

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.480
Forgive me, Arque.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.950
If I may point out,

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:28.320
in these conditions, there is no
difference between humans and us A.I.s.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.720
You don't know when to zip it, either, Tarbo.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:31.910
Forgive me.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.250
So, this is Shizuno...

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.630
Meta... body?

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.270
Literally, a "phantom body."

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:48.060
That's what all the humans in this world are called.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.310
So, you're saying I'm a phantom?
Does that mean I don't exist?!

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.000
Then what's this "me" that's here now?!

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:57.640
That depends on your definition of existence.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:04.550
Where am I?

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:11.350
I'm afraid there are limits on
what I may tell you as well.

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:14.560
Am I a phantom? Answer me, Lemures!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.370
Cogito ergo sum.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:22.470
"I think, therefore, I am."

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:24.640
Don't go throwing Descartes in my face here!

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.340
"To exist is to be perceived."

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:30.000
Berkeley's out of date, too! Now cut it out!

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:34.540
I'm glad. Our conversations
were always spirited like this.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:39.590
I'm possessed by a dead man.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:43.890
I feel like a ghost lecturing on
the immortality of the soul.

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:46.790
"Ghost" is an excellent way to put it.

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:50.330
A bit literary, but a good definition of a meta-body.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.730
Kyo Sogoru.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:57.570
You skipped over the dialectic process
to reach a deeper understanding.

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.010
Do you understand why?

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:03.840
Because I'm not learning anything,
just remembering things I've forgotten.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.600
If you understand that,
then why are you asking questions?

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:08.850
Because normally, this is impossible!

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.290
And yet you already understand
that the situation is far from normal.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.520
But it's impossible!

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:19.290
Knowledge is unhappiness.
The man who knows much knows a terrible truth,

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.300
and he cannot turn away from it.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.920
Pascal, now?

00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:27.370
And him... What was he, then?

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:28.700
That guy Abyss.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.840
A Gards-orm Reconstructant.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.640
"Reconstructant?" What's that?!

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:35.310
The enemy.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:48.750
All right, I'll answer any questions
within available parameters.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:56.490
Correct. The empty apartments were
once occupied by many Cerebrants.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:13:00.060
However, more than half have been
killed in the battle with the Gards-orm.

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:05.340
Why don't you ever see your mother? Well...

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:09.240
Not seeing her doesn't really affect your life, does it?

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:16.120
<i>It's here, in this world.</i>

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:22.680
Commander Shima? No, he won't come.
Everyone's on the Oceanus.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:26.950
<i>Fine with me. I don't want to</i>
<i>have anything to do with him.</i>

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:32.730
You'll be having your first end of term exam soon,
but it won't be different from middle school.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.040
Let's just relax for this one.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.110
Okay, let's hit the basics today.

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:41.560
<i>Ghosts. Phantoms. Everyone's artificial.</i>

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:44.010
<i>Kurage, too.</i>

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.780
<i>Them, too.</i>

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:48.710
<i>Even Kaminagi?</i>

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:09.770
Not bad, Mizuki. I wish you would join the swim club.

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:11.570
I'm not that serious about it.

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:13.230
Didn't you see before?

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:14.680
See what?

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:17.310
There's something weird about that Sogoru guy.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:19.480
He was walking along with a scary look on his face.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:21.880
Really? He was normal this morning.

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:24.550
Maybe he puts on an act in front of you, Ryoko.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:26.950
Why?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.050
You know...

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:31.390
Oh! It's Kaori! There she goes!

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:40.600
Kyo, you son of a!

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.930
Don't mess with me today!

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:49.480
There it is. Blood...

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:51.910
Of course it is.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:54.270
Naturally, because I'm human.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.190
What's with him? He's not himself.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.350
Hm? Yeah...

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:03.590
It's not at the same level as when
he fights about the swim club.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:08.800
July 9th, 1943.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.770
At Akutan Island in the Aleutians...

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:15.640
the U.S. Navy sighted a Type-21 Zero, till then an
unbeatable fighter wrapped in a veil of mystery,

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.870
making an emergency landing.

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:22.810
After thoroughly testing and analyzing it,

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.550
they discovered numerous techniques
to counter the Zero in combat.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.070
destroying the legend of its invincibility.

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:32.790
Well, that's basically why an enemy
tries to steal data on anything.

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:34.280
I figured that.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:36.490
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:37.560
You do?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.990
But, there's no scene like that in the Zega game...

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.860
Wha?! What's up?

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.230
You really are a nice guy.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:46.830
No way you're a ghost or a phantom.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.140
Oh!

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:49.000
What?

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:50.660
Don't look over here!

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:52.940
Your cheek looks really bad.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:54.130
Ugh...

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:59.270
Will you fight?

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:03.040
Even when the world suddenly
crumbles before your eyes?

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:06.220
This is the true story of
what happened 40 years later.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.620
Welcome, to the future of the world.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.990
<i>Something really is wrong with him...</i>

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:18.490
Ugh...

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.760
Kaminagi. Wanna go for a walk?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.730
Uh... Sure! Let me get ready!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:44.190
<i>The unidentified armed vehicles which attacked</i>
<i>the United Nations vehicles yesterday...</i>

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:48.030
<i>were later determined to have been</i>
<i>trying to steal military secrets.</i>

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.590
<i>Security forces have taken</i>
<i>countermeasures and are in pursuit of them.</i>

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.660
Exactly!

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:57.670
There's a very direct link between
this world and the other one.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.270
You don't see them because
you don't need to see them.

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:06.150
For those who do need to see them,

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.120
the shop keeper and the customers exist.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:10.940
I'll just leave the money here.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:17.750
Sorry for the wait.

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:19.620
Hm? Right...

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.300
Does your cheek still hurt?

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:26.530
Nah.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.330
It's so quiet.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.110
Tell me, Kaminagi...

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:38.710
You really are "you," aren't you?

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:39.680
Aren't you?

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:45.220
What the hell am I saying?

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:46.280
Screw this!

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:55.160
Look! You can see Tokyo!

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:58.800
Of course you can see it.
It's right next to us.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:00.200
<i>Tokyo!</i>

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:07.030
I was thinking... Next semester...

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:09.700
I promised Mizuki I'd go hang
out with her in Shibuya.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:12.640
I suppose we could go on summer break,

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:16.440
but for some reason,
I feel like I won't be able to go then.

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:19.280
We'd take that train there.

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:21.720
Let's go now!

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:23.820
You idiot!

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:24.790
Let's go!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.160
Wait!

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:36.460
No, we shouldn't!
It's late! We'll do it next time!

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:38.740
What's with you? We're not little kids!

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.600
We'll come right back!

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.800
But... I get the feeling we shouldn't go there!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.880
Don't go!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.620
Never mind. I'll go by myself.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:52.610
Kyo!

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:17.310
<i>As far as I remember, I haven't left</i>
<i>Maihama since I entered high school.</i>

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.990
<i>I'll go see it.</i>
<i>I'll see the city from outside.</i>

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.650
<i>And when I do, it'll all become clear!</i>

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:29.990
<i>I'll see we're not phantoms!</i>
<i>Not constructs! That we aren't ghosts!</i>

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:57.580
Kaminagi...

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:09.920
It's impossible...

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:14.270
It's impossible... All of this...

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:15.570
It's no use.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:17.540
Shizuno-sempai!

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:19.840
You can't go "outside the city."

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:22.570
It just doesn't exist.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:27.310
The world we inhabit is a closed
world of only "here" and "now."

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:29.250
That's a lie!

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:40.350
Is that what you want me to say?!

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:42.950
It's true!

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:47.190
Maihama city is a virtual world that exists
only within a quantum computer server!

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:53.130
And we live within the quantum servers as
meta-bodies because we've lost our physical bodies!

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.600
Personality and memory data constructs.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:00.780
The human race was destroyed by the Gards-orm.

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:04.750
Not a single living human is left on Earth!

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:06.150
Hold on here!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:10.990
All of us are living in a phantom
city that's inside a machine!

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:13.460
The memories of a dead human race!

00:21:17.930 --> 00:21:19.190
That was mean of me.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.170
If what you just told me is true...

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:26.970
Then when I open my eyes,
all these false things will!

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.340
No, don't!

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:31.000
It'll all disappear!

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:45.990
Are "here" and "now" the only
things that we can accept?

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.450
Oh man, Kaminagi...

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:06.210
You and me both...

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:08.080
We're just phantoms.

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:54.500
Kyo really seems sad lately.

00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:56.260
It's like he's covering something up.

00:22:56.260 --> 00:22:59.290
You don't think Shizuno-sempai
rejected him, do you?!

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:02.070
It's so hard, seeing Kyo so sad.

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:04.200
How can I just stand by and watch?

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:07.130
I know! Kyo, come location
hunting with me!

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:10.580
